@page "/"

<PageTitle>TRM Cosmology UI</PageTitle>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h4" GutterBottom="true">TRM Cosmology UI</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
    This interface compares GR-baseline predictions against TRM model outputs across quantum, weak-field, strong-field, and cosmological regimes.
</MudText>

<MudPaper Class="pa-4 mb-3" Outlined="true">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" GutterBottom="true">How to read each dashboard</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">1) Set parameters in the left control panel.</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">2) Review the Physics Context box for formulas and current parameter values.</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">3) Compare chart/table outputs between GR reference and TRM prediction.</MudText>
</MudPaper>

<MudPaper Class="pa-4" Outlined="true">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" GutterBottom="true">Common reference formulas (weak field)</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">GR redshift: Δν/ν ≈ ΔΦ / c²</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">GR deflection: Δθ ≈ 4GM / (c² b)</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">GR perihelion: Δω = 6πGM / (c² a(1-e²))</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="mt-2">Use the navigation menu to open regime-specific pages for detailed TRM formulas and live parameter readouts.</MudText>
</MudPaper>
